 antidepressant properties of the Atypical antipsychotic Quetiapine</article-title><conf-name>Poster presented at APANR336</conf-name><fpage>142</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ndt-3-847"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goodwin</surname><given-names>FK</given-names></name><name><surname>Jamison</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1990</year><source>Manic-depressive illness</source><publisher-loc>New York, NY</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ndt-3-847"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hamilton</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1960</year><article-title>A rating scale for depression</article-title><source>J Neurol Neurosurg Psychiatry</source><volume>23</volume><fpage>56</fpage><lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14399272</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-ndt-3-847"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Himmelhoch</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Thase</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>allinger</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1991</year><article-title>Tranylcypromine versus imipramine in anergic bipolar depression</article-title><source>Am J Psychiatry</source><volume>148</volume><fpage>910</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2053632</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-ndt-3-847"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hlastala</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Malinger</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Bipolar depression: an underestimated treatment chal